---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy: what carbsaresugar.com does and does not collect"
  description="The privacy policy for carbsaresugar.com: the site sets no cookies or storage; the two third-party scripts are Google AdSense and Cloudflare Web Analytics."
>
  <PageIntro slot="intro" title="Privacy policy" lede="Last updated 21 September 2026." />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 sm:py-14">
    <div class="prose-body">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Summary</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no accounts, no forms and no database. Page views are counted by Cloudflare Web Analytics, which
        the host runs without cookies, described under Analytics below. The site's own code does not set cookies, does not
        write to your browser's storage and does not send anything you do on the page to a server. The other third party is
        Google AdSense, which serves the advertising, does use cookies and browser storage, and has its own data
        practices, described below.
      </p>
      <p>
        This policy was written from a check of the site's built code, not from a template. The results of that check are
        listed in the next section.
      </p>

      <h2>What was checked</h2>
      <p>Before this policy was published, the built site was inspected for the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Network requests made by the site's code:</strong> none. The calculator's food list is bundled into the page,
          and the site's scripts contain no fetch, XMLHttpRequest, WebSocket or beacon calls. Adding, removing and totalling
          foods happens entirely in your browser. Separately, the host, Cloudflare, adds its own page-view counter to every
          page as it is served, described under Analytics below.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Browser storage:</strong> the site's code does not use localStorage, sessionStorage, IndexedDB or cookies.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Server-side code:</strong> none. The site is a set of static files. There are no API routes or server
          functions that could receive data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fonts:</strong> served from this site's own domain, not from a font service.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Third-party scripts:</strong> one in the site's own code, the Google AdSense script loaded from
          pagead2.googlesyndication.com. No other third-party script, stylesheet, font or image is referenced in the site's
          pages. Cloudflare adds a second script as it serves each page, the Web Analytics beacon loaded from
          static.cloudflareinsights.com, covered under Analytics below.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The page was also loaded and used in a real browser with every storage write and network request recorded. The
        site's own code made no requests and wrote nothing. Cloudflare's Web Analytics beacon loaded from
        static.cloudflareinsights.com and reported the page view. The AdSense script, once loaded, did the following on
        its own:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          it requested resources from pagead2.googlesyndication.com, googleads.g.doubleclick.net, www.google.com,
          ep1.adtrafficquality.google and ep2.adtrafficquality.google;
        </li>
        <li>it wrote and removed a test entry in localStorage (named <code>__storage_test__</code>);</li>
        <li>it set a test cookie (named <code>TESTCOOKIESENABLED</code>) to check whether cookies are enabled;</li>
        <li>
          a cookie named <code>IDE</code> was set on Google's doubleclick.net domain, which Google uses for advertising.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>After the session, no entries remained in this site's localStorage or sessionStorage, and no cookie was set on this site's own domain.</p>
      <p>
        In live use, AdSense may set further cookies and contact further Google domains depending on your location, your
        consent choices and the ads being served. Those are controlled by Google, not by this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Your food list and the page address</h2>
      <p>
        When you add foods, the calculator writes your list into the page address, for example
        <code>?f=banana:1</code>. This is how bookmarking and sharing work without an account. The list is not saved anywhere
        else by this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        Two consequences are worth knowing. Anyone you share the link with can see the list. And when a page address with a
        list in it is loaded, the full address, including the list, is requested from the web host, just as any web address
        is. Changes you make after the page has loaded are not sent anywhere.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request information, such
        as IP addresses and the pages requested, to deliver the site and protect it from abuse. Cloudflare also counts page
        views for this site, described under Analytics below. Cloudflare's handling of that information is covered by the
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Page views are counted with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which Cloudflare runs as part of hosting this site. It is
        added to the page by Cloudflare as the page is served, so it does not appear in this site's own code.
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare states</a> that it "does not use any client-side
        state, such as cookies or localStorage, to collect usage metrics" and does not "fingerprint" individuals by IP
        address or User Agent string. It gives this site page-view totals, not information about you.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising: Google AdSense</h2>
      <p>
        The site shows ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to serve
        ads based on your visits to this site and other sites, to limit how often an ad is shown, and to measure ad
        performance. Where the law requires it, Google may show a consent message before using cookies for these purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>,
        and you can turn off personalised advertising at
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">adssettings.google.com</a>. Blocking third-party scripts in your browser
        stops the AdSense script from loading; the calculator works without it.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you write to the contact address, your email and address are received in an ordinary email inbox. They are used
        only to reply and to act on corrections, and they are not added to any mailing list or shared.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The site is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect information from anyone.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If the site's code changes in a way that affects anything above, for example by adding a new third-party service,
        this page will be updated before or at the same time as that change, and the date at the top will change.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:vetorainfo@gmail.com">vetorainfo@gmail.com</a><!--/email_off-->.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
